  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new subdivision to N.D.C.C. 54-12-14(1)): For costs associated with class 1 exempt licenses under section 62.1-04-03.2.\nSection 2 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(2)(n)): A North Dakota member of the Congress of the United States who maintains the same level of firearms proficiency as is required by the peace officer standards and training board for law enforcement officers. A local law enforcement agency shall issue a certificate of compliance under this subdivision to an individual who is proficient and the individual shall file the certificate with the bureau of criminal investigation;\nSection 2 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-05(2)(o)): An individual who possesses a valid class 1 exempt license under section 62.1-04-03.2;\nSection 3 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-04-03.2(1)): The director of the bureau of criminal investigation shall issue a class 1 exempt license to carry a firearm or dangerous weapon concealed to an individual who: a. Possesses a valid class 1 firearm license under section 62.1-04-03; and b. Successfully completes the training and testing requirements under this section.\nSection 3 (N.D.C.C. 62.1-04-03.2(3)): The bureau of criminal investigation shall develop and administer an annual training requirement for holders of a class 1 exempt license which may include classroom and field training components."
}